      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Ingestion path",
      "items": ["Upload persists a document record and chunks in PostgreSQL, then saves vectors and metadata to the local FAISS store.", "The synchronous upload handler uses loader → cleaner → paragraph chunker before Jina embedding."]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Query / RAG path",
      "items": ["/ask verifies ownership, records messages, embeds the question, searches FAISS, logs ranked results, and builds the prompt.", "Groq receives retrieved context, history, and question through model openai/gpt-oss-120b."]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust and persistence",
      "items": ["Protected routes use HTTP Bearer JWT (HS256) and validate the active user; document and conversation ownership is enforced in route handlers.", "Jina and Groq are external HTTPS services called with runtime API keys; FAISS and upload files are local filesystem state."]
    }
